	“give me a date and location and show the sky,” these are more practical:

	| Option | Type | Notes |
	|--------|------|-------|
	| **Stellarium** | Free / open-source | Best match. Desktop version has a **Remote Control plugin** with a full HTTP API (runs on localhost). You can set location, date/time, view direction, and trigger screenshots. Also has scripting support. |
	| **Stellarium Web / Web Engine** | Free | Web version accepts URL parameters for location/date; the JavaScript engine can be embedded. |
	| **starplot** (Python) | Free library | Excellent for generating customizable star charts (zenith charts, horizon charts, etc.) from an observer’s lat/lon + datetime. Outputs SVG/PNG. |
	| **Starmap360 API** | Commercial | Explicitly designed for this: date + lat/lon/time → SVG or PNG star map. |
	| Online generators | Free web tools | Sites such as Starlight Tools or Skylit Studio generate maps in the browser from date/location. |

